<h2>Catechist Guide</h2>
<p class="big-question">For preparing and leading the class. For the catechist's use only.</p>

<h3>Class Summary</h3>

<p><strong>Estimated duration:</strong> 60 minutes</p>
<p><strong>Central theme:</strong> Sacramentals are sacred signs that extend the grace of the sacraments into daily life. Christian funerals celebrate the Passover of the deceased: their passage from death to eternal life with the risen Christ.</p>
<p><strong>Objectives:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Distinguish between sacraments and sacramentals.</li>
<li>Learn the types of sacramentals and their biblical foundation.</li>
<li>Appreciate popular piety as a treasure of the people's faith.</li>
<li>Understand the Christian meaning of death and the parts of funerals.</li>
<li>Connect faith with cultural traditions around honoring the dead and blessing homes.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Key verse:</strong> "Listen, I will tell you a mystery! We will not all die, but we will all be changed" (1 Cor 15:51)</p>
<p><strong>Catechism references:</strong> CCC 1667-1690</p>

</section>

